Usage: pathchk [OPTION] NAME...

Check whether file names are valid or portable.
Check that each file name is valid for the current filesystem,
and optionally check for POSIX portability.

OPTIONS:
  -p                 check for most POSIX systems
  -P                 check for empty names and leading dash
      --portability  check for all POSIX systems (equivalent to -p -P)
      --help         display this help and exit
  -V, --version      output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
